WEBVTT

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:02.547
History has a pulse.

00:00:03.600 --> 00:00:04.947
Just listen.

00:00:04.947 --> 00:00:09.000
[Press machinery, unaccompanied]

00:00:09.300 --> 00:00:18.402
In seventeen seventy-six, the Declaration entered a print shop.
The words had to reach the people.

00:00:19.100 --> 00:00:24.998
The spirit of printing transforms a working draft into a printed
sheet.

00:00:25.600 --> 00:00:28.433
And a voice carried farther.

00:00:28.900 --> 00:00:34.426
The inheritance of printing reaches beyond the founding of
America.

00:00:35.100 --> 00:00:37.097
The search for wisdom.

00:00:38.700 --> 00:00:40.836
The call to mercy.

00:00:43.200 --> 00:00:45.894
The courage to find our way.

00:00:47.200 --> 00:00:53.051
Here in Austin, we give enduring words a place on the page.

00:00:55.200 --> 00:01:02.027
Ink. Paper. A working press. A tradition, carried forward.

00:01:02.700 --> 00:01:04.372
Read the words.

00:01:05.100 --> 00:01:06.679
Keep the source.

00:01:07.100 --> 00:01:09.701
Make room for the enduring.

00:01:10.100 --> 00:01:12.701
Thomas Broadside Company.

00:01:12.900 --> 00:01:14.943
Words to live with.
